        },
        {
          "id": "doc-3947a328a770::sentence-231",
          "documentId": "doc-3947a328a770",
          "text": "I would also like to point out that there are many more what may be called 'secondary COVID-19 deaths' that are related to the conditions caused by the virus, but not directly due to infection from the virus. ",
          "start": 8891,
          "end": 9100,
          "contextSpans": [
            {
              "id": "doc-3947a328a770::sentence-230",
              "documentId": "doc-3947a328a770",
              "text": "A major confounding variable in any current COVID-19 mortality study will be the change in definitions of the COVID-19 cause of death by the WHO and on death certifications midstream through this pandemic. ",
              "start": 8685,
              "end": 8891,
              "direction": "PREVIOUS"
            }
          ],
          "context": "A major confounding variable in any current COVID-19 mortality study will be the change in definitions of the COVID-19 cause of death by the WHO and on death certifications midstream through this pandemic. I would also like to point out that there are many more what may be called 'secondary COVID-19 deaths' that are related to the conditions caused by the virus, but not directly due to infection from the virus."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-3947a328a770::sentence-61",
          "documentId": "doc-3947a328a770",
          "text": "Excess Deaths From COVID-19, Community Bereavement, and Restorative Justice for Communities of ColorViewpointOctober 20, 2020This Viewpoint discusses ways the COVID-19 pandemic has compounded existing health, human rights, and economic disparities in communities of color and proposes a program of restorative justice in response, comprising investments in education and housing, reforms in lending practices and criminal justice, and more.Lisa A. Cooper, MD, MPH; David R. Williams, PhD, MPH\n",
          "start": 2698,
          "end": 3191,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "Excess Deaths From COVID-19, Community Bereavement, and Restorative Justice for Communities of ColorViewpointOctober 20, 2020This Viewpoint discusses ways the COVID-19 pandemic has compounded existing health, human rights, and economic disparities in communities of color and proposes a program of restorative justice in response, comprising investments in education and housing, reforms in lending practices and criminal justice, and more.Lisa A. Cooper, MD, MPH; David R. Williams, PhD, MPH"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-3947a328a770::sentence-360",
          "documentId": "doc-3947a328a770",
          "text": "Between March 1, 2020, and April 25, 2020, a total of 505 059 deaths were reported in the US; 87 001 (95% CI, 86 578-87 423) were excess deaths, of which 56 246 (65%) were attributed to COVID-19. ",
          "start": 18780,
          "end": 18976,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "Between March 1, 2020, and April 25, 2020, a total of 505 059 deaths were reported in the US; 87 001 (95% CI, 86 578-87 423) were excess deaths, of which 56 246 (65%) were attributed to COVID-19."
        }
      ]
    },
